e $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $g(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =(\\frac{∂g}{∂x})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(\\frac{∂g}{∂y})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=- 2 x y - y^{2},\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=- x^{2} - 2 x y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =- r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =- 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =(- r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2696e2e-7aa9-5831-9028-9adfe5889bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Cartesian Function With Respect to Plane Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0280772c-4d86-54c4-9ab1-42cbec9f9517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526157} {:answer/id #uuid "9306357a-dd3a-55a8-86f4-13d69d861185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526195} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1045dc-ae7b-53d6-a201-09fd8a333326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526198} {:answer/id #uuid "ab089900-ab5c-58c7-b4fc-284ea3c05606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526203} {:answer/id #uuid "e746cd53-7432-5738-9ad8-542080a2827e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9306357a-dd3a-55a8-86f4-13d69d861185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526195} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd9e72c-be44-595b-952d-4e4727b9d32d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8479fa83-fbbd-5793-b8d0-0b7149751139" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} y + 3 x y^{2},$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=- 4 x y + 3 y^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=- 2 x^{2} + 6 x y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta} & =(3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =- 3 r^{3} \\sin^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{3} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 6 r^{3} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r^{3} \\cos^{3}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2696e2e-7aa9-5831-9028-9adfe5889bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Cartesian Function With Respect to Plane Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4b70f1-a2a9-50cf-83a8-2af7e51db9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 14 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526165} {:answer/id #uuid "25451830-b3c4-5ed7-907b-8021140d7082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526168} {:answer/id #uuid "80d2b349-1aa9-5707-a1f3-27d64fedfcb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\rig